+### Modal classes
+
+The modal key ships whole: the modal and its dialog, the content with its header, title, body, and
+footer, the close control the header places, the backdrop, the static bounce, the scrollable and
+centered dialogs, the dialog sizes, and the fullscreen classes. Each state is a class set in
+markup, and § Compatibility records the plugin that opens a dialog, closes it, and holds focus
+inside it as an engine obligation.
+
+No Veneer rule shows a modal. The `.modal` rule hides it, and an engine writes its `display` style
+inline when it opens the dialog. An engine also sets the `modal-open` class on the document body
+while a dialog is open, and no Veneer rule reads that class.
+
+A shown modal covers its containing block as a fixed layer that scrolls its own overflow. The
+`.modal-dialog` rule lets the pointer through to the modal and the `.modal-content` rule takes the
+pointer back, so a press beside the content lands on the modal. The `.modal-dialog` rule applies
+the `--bs-modal-margin` variable as the dialog's margin: the `.modal` rule sets that variable to the
+`--vn-space-4` token below the `sm` boundary and to the release's literal `1.75rem` length from that
+boundary up. From the `sm` boundary up, the `.modal-dialog` rule also applies the
+`--bs-modal-width` variable as the dialog's cap and centers the dialog. The `.modal` rule sets that
+variable to a `500px` width. On the dialog, the `.modal-sm` class sets it to a `300px` width from
+the `sm` boundary, the `.modal-lg` and `.modal-xl` classes set it to an `800px` width from the `lg`
+boundary, and the `.modal-xl` class sets it to a `1140px` width from the `xl` boundary. The widths
+and the wide margin stay literal, because no published Veneer scale resolves to them.
+
+The `.modal-content` rule lays the header, the body, and the footer out as a column. It paints the
+text from the `--bs-body-color` alias, the fill from the `--bs-body-bg` alias, and the edge from the
+`--bs-border-color-translucent` alias, and the header and footer rules paint their dividers from the
+`--bs-border-color` alias, so a modal inside a dark island paints the island's values. The content's
+corners read the `--bs-border-radius-lg` variable, and the header and footer rules round their outer
+corners one border width inside them. The `.modal` rule sets the body, header, and footer insets to
+the `--vn-space-8` token and the footer gap to the `--vn-space-4` token. The `.modal-body`,
+`.modal-header`, and `.modal-footer` rules apply the insets, and the `.modal-footer > *` rule
+applies the gap, so the `--vn-factor-density` factor moves every inset, the gap, and the narrow
+margin together. The footer lays its children out one gap apart at its end. The release declares
+the footer's fill variable with no value, so the footer paints the content's own fill. The
+`.modal-title` rule reads its line height from the `--bs-modal-title-line-height` variable, which
+the `.modal` rule sets to the `--vn-line-body` token.
+
+The close control inside the header takes half the header's inset as its padding and gives it back
+through negative margins, so its target grows without moving the header's edge, and its automatic
+start margin pushes it to the header's end. The rule selects the control through the `.modal-header`
+class, so a close control in the body keeps its own box. § Close classes gives the control's own
+treatment.
+
+The backdrop is fixed across the viewport and paints the `--vn-palette-black-base` token. It is
+transparent while it carries the `fade` class alone, and it paints at its `0.5` opacity when it
+also carries the `show` class, which is the pair an engine writes as it fades the backdrop in. The
+`overlay-backdrop` mixin in the `src/styles/_mixins.scss` file writes that treatment from the
+stacking level, the fill, and the opacity it is given.
+
+The `.modal` rule sets the `--bs-modal-zindex` variable to the `--vn-stack-dialog-base` token and
+applies it as the modal's `z-index` property. The `.modal-backdrop` rule sets the
+`--bs-backdrop-zindex` variable to the `--vn-stack-dialog-backdrop` token, and the
+`overlay-backdrop` mixin applies it as the backdrop's `z-index` property. So a retuned dialog rung
+moves every modal, and a retuned backdrop rung moves every backdrop.
+
+The `.modal-dialog-scrollable` class holds the dialog to the modal's height less its margins, and
+the body scrolls between the header and the footer. The `.modal-dialog-centered` class centers the
+dialog in the modal. A dialog inside a modal carrying the `fade` class rests at a `50px` offset
+above its place, and it moves into place when the modal also carries the `show` class. The move
+takes the release's literal `0.3s` duration, because no published motion token resolves to it, and
+the `transition` mixin writes it, so the move resolves to no transition under the reduced-motion
+preference. The `modal-static` class, which an engine sets for a moment when a dialog refuses to
+close, scales the dialog to a `1.02` factor.
+
+Each fullscreen class fills the viewport with the dialog, drops the content's edge and corners, and
+scrolls the body. The `.modal-fullscreen` class does so at every width, and each
+`.modal-fullscreen-{infix}-down` class does so below its infix's boundary alone, so the
+`.modal-fullscreen-md-down` class fills the viewport below a `768px` width.
+
+These are the key's recorded departures.
+
+- **The stacking levels read Veneer's ladder.** The release writes the `1055` level for the modal
+  and the `1050` level for the backdrop; Veneer writes the `var(--vn-stack-dialog-base)` and
+  `var(--vn-stack-dialog-backdrop)` values, which resolve to the same levels.
+- **The insets, the narrow margin, and the footer gap read Veneer's density scale.** The release
+  writes a `1rem` length for the body and header insets and a `0.5rem` length for the narrow margin
+  and the footer gap; Veneer writes the `--vn-space-8` and `--vn-space-4` tokens, which already
+  resolve to those lengths. The header's combined inset, the `1rem 1rem` value in the release, is
+  written as the `--vn-space-8` token on each axis.
+- **The title's line height reads the body rhythm.** The recorded `1.5` value becomes the
+  `var(--vn-line-body)` value, which resolves to the same number.
+- **The backdrop paints the black token.** The recorded `#000` value becomes the
+  `var(--vn-palette-black-base)` value, which holds the same bytes.
+
+The showcase's Modal region renders a shown dialog over its backdrop, the static bounce, a
+scrollable and a centered dialog, each dialog size, and each fullscreen class, each inside the
+shell's `viewport` frame. Each modal carries the `d-block` utility in place of the `display` style
+an engine writes inline, beside the `fade` and `show` classes an opened dialog carries. The shown
+dialog alone renders its backdrop, as a sibling of its modal inside the frame. Each dialog carries
+the `dialog` role and no `aria-modal` attribute, because a dialog rendered at rest traps nothing and
+the rest of the showcase stays reachable, and each dialog is named by its title. Each close control
+is named by its `aria-label` attribute. No specimen renders a backdrop carrying the `fade` class
+alone: that backdrop paints nothing, so its frame would be the frame of the dialog without it, and
+the capture registry declines it.
+
+The `tests/src/styles/components/modal.test.ts` proof reads each resolved treatment in the browser:
+the written selectors, the hidden and the shown modal, the stacking levels and a wrapper retuning
+them, each space slot and the density factor, the content's column and its paint in light and
+inside a dark island, the header's close control beside a control in the body and under a retune
+of the header's inset, each dialog cap one pixel below and at each boundary, each fullscreen class
+below and at its boundary, the centered and the scrollable dialogs, the entrance and the settled
+dialog under the staged reduced-motion preference, the static bounce, and the backdrop's fading and
+shown opacity.
